    "html": "<p>Nitrobase includes a built-in <strong>Model Context Protocol (MCP)</strong> server at <code>/api/mcp</code> (stateless <strong>Streamable HTTP</strong> transport, JSON responses, single JSON-RPC message per <code>POST</code>), authenticated with the same <code>nbk_...</code> API tokens as the REST API.</p>\n<h2>Connecting Claude Code</h2>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">claude</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> mcp</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> add</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> --transport</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> http</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> nitrobase</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> https://panel.example.com/api/mcp</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  --header</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"Authorization: Bearer nbk_...\"</span></span></code></pre>\n<h2>Connecting Cursor or Other MCP Clients</h2>\n<p>Add the server to your <strong>user-level</strong> MCP config (for example <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-json\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"mcpServers\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">    \"nitrobase\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">      \"url\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"https://panel.example.com/api/mcp\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">      \"headers\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">        \"Authorization\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Bearer nbk_...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">      }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<div class=\"docCallout docCallout-caution\"><div class=\"docCalloutHeader\"><span class=\"docCalloutBadge\">CAUTION</span><span class=\"docCalloutTitle\">Never Commit API Tokens</span></div><div class=\"docCalloutContent\">\n<p>An MCP JSON config containing an <code>nbk_...</code> token holds a live secret. Keep it in your user-level config (such as <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>)—never in a repository's <code>.mcp.json</code>, and never commit it to Git. <code>claude mcp add</code> stores credentials in your local Claude Code config.</p>\n</div></div>\n<p>In the Nitrobase UI, <strong>Settings → API tokens</strong> provides a <strong>Connect an AI agent</strong> panel with ready-to-copy snippets for Claude Code and JSON MCP clients (pre-filled during a new token's one-time reveal).</p>\n<h2>Recommended Token Presets</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI agent (read-only):</strong> Grants <code>server.view</code>, <code>app.view</code>, <code>backup.view</code>, and <code>monitoring.view</code>. Exposes all read-only tools (<code>list_servers</code>, <code>get_server</code>, <code>get_server_health</code>, <code>get_server_metrics</code>, <code>list_apps</code>, <code>get_app</code>, <code>get_app_env</code>, <code>get_app_logs</code>, <code>list_app_deployments</code>, <code>list_templates</code>, <code>list_template_versions</code>, <code>list_app_backups</code>, <code>list_backup_destinations</code>, <code>list_jobs</code>, <code>get_job</code>) except <code>preflight_app</code> (which needs <code>app.deploy</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>AI agent (operator):</strong> Adds <code>app.deploy</code> and <code>backup.create</code>, enabling <code>preflight_app</code>, <code>create_app</code>, <code>deploy_app</code>, <code>redeploy_app</code>, <code>start_app</code>, <code>stop_app</code>, <code>restart_app</code>, and <code>backup_app</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How MCP Tools Work</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Auto-generated from REST:</strong> Every non-streaming <code>/api/v1</code> route becomes a snake_case MCP tool (<code>listApps</code> → <code>list_apps</code>, <code>deployApp</code> → <code>deploy_app</code>, <code>getJob</code> → <code>get_job</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Permission-scoped visibility:</strong> An agent only sees the tools its token is permitted to call.</li>\n<li><strong>Safety annotations:</strong> Read-only tools are marked <code>readOnlyHint: true</code>; mutating tools are marked <code>destructiveHint: true</code> (except <code>backup_app</code>, which is non-destructive), prompting most MCP clients to ask for confirmation before running them.</li>\n<li><strong>Async jobs:</strong> Tools that start background work return a job ID (<code>deploymentId</code>)—agents poll <code>get_job</code> until completion.</li>\n<li><strong>Full auditing &#x26; rate limiting:</strong> Every tool call runs through the same rate limiter and audit logger as REST requests, tagged with <code>channel: mcp</code>.</li>\n</ul>"
