    "html": "<p>Nitrobase ships with a built-in marketplace of curated open-source templates defined under <code>templates/</code>. Each template generates strong secrets automatically, passes through Nitrobase's compose security policy, and comes with app-aware backup and health-check configuration.</p>\n<h2>Available Marketplace Templates</h2>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th align=\"left\">Template</th><th align=\"left\">Category</th><th align=\"left\">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Supabase</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Backend</td><td align=\"left\">Full Postgres platform: database, GoTrue Auth, PostgREST, Realtime, Storage, Edge Functions, and Studio. Supports importing from and exporting to Supabase Cloud.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Appwrite</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Backend</td><td align=\"left\">Auth, databases, storage, messaging, realtime, and Appwrite Console (note: Functions/Sites runtime executor is disabled for host security because it requires Docker socket access). Supports Appwrite Cloud import/export.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>PocketBase</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Backend</td><td align=\"left\">Single-binary backend built from verified official release checksums: realtime SQLite database, auth, file storage, and Admin UI (<code>/_/</code>).</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Standalone Database</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Database</td><td align=\"left\">Managed PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB, Valkey, or MongoDB with web console, connection strings, and app linking.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>n8n</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Automation</td><td align=\"left\">Workflow automation with 400+ integrations, code steps, and AI agents on Postgres (owner account and encryption key managed automatically).</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Plausible</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Analytics</td><td align=\"left\">Privacy-first web analytics on ClickHouse and PostgreSQL (official CE version branches).</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Umami</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Analytics</td><td align=\"left\">Cookie-free web analytics on PostgreSQL (default admin password automatically rotated on first boot).</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>RustFS</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Storage</td><td align=\"left\">Apache-2.0 S3-compatible object storage with S3 API on the primary domain and web console on <code>console.&#x3C;domain></code>.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>From Git Repository</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Custom</td><td align=\"left\">Build and deploy your own code from a Git branch using Dockerfile, Railpack, or Static site builders.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Custom Compose</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Custom</td><td align=\"left\">Paste any <code>docker-compose.yml</code> and deploy it under the same safety policy and backup engine.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Deployment Flow</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Apps → New App</strong> and select a template.</li>\n<li>Pick a ready <strong>Server</strong> and choose a <strong>Version</strong> (pinned to a commit SHA at deploy time for reproducible redeploys).</li>\n<li>Configure optional <strong>Custom domain</strong> (leave empty for an automatic free <code>*.sslip.io</code> HTTPS domain) and editable environment variables.</li>\n<li>Nitrobase runs a <strong>Pre-flight check</strong> validating server readiness, disk/RAM limits, ports, domain availability, and compose policy before creating anything.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Deploy</strong>. Nitrobase writes <code>/etc/nitrobase/apps/&#x3C;folder>/</code>, pulls images, starts containers, attaches routed services to <code>nitrobase-network</code>, runs HTTP health &#x26; stability checks, and displays generated credentials in the app's <strong>Credentials</strong> panel.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Post-Deploy Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Environment Editor:</strong> Edit variables with automatic secret masking; <code>initial_only</code> variables freeze after first deploy; <code>rotatable</code> secrets can be regenerated (with optional post-rotation SQL hooks) and redeployed in one click.</li>\n<li><strong>Resource Limits:</strong> Override per-service memory limits, soft reservations, and CPU cores.</li>\n<li><strong>Published Ports:</strong> Opt-in host port publishing for templates that declare <code>[[ports]]</code> (off by default, configured under <strong>Settings → Published ports</strong>).</li>\n<li><strong>Scheduled Tasks:</strong> Run recurring cron jobs inside any app container (<strong>Tasks</strong> tab, up to 20 tasks per app, minimum 5-minute interval).</li>\n</ul>"
