    "locale": "en",
    "section": "backup-recovery",
    "html": "<p>In addition to backing up your apps, Nitrobase backs up its own PostgreSQL control-plane database (servers, apps, encrypted credentials, domains, schedules, audit logs, and team configuration) under <strong>Data → Backups</strong> (requires <code>instance.manage</code> permission, available to Instance Administrators).</p>\n<h2>What a Self-Backup Contains</h2>\n<p>Each self-backup is uploaded as <code>nitrobase/&#x3C;date>-&#x3C;id>.tar.gz.enc</code> along with a recorded SHA-256 checksum:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>PostgreSQL dump (<code>nitrobase.sql</code>):</strong> Full logical dump created with <code>pg_dump</code> (<code>SELF_BACKUP_PG_DUMP</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Manifest:</strong> Metadata including schema/app version, timestamp, and instance marker.</li>\n<li><strong>Portable OpenSSL Encryption:</strong> Gzipped tar archive encrypted using OpenSSL <code>aes-256-cbc</code> with PBKDF2-SHA256 (<code>SELF_BACKUP_PBKDF2_ITERATIONS=200000</code>) and your <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Mandatory Pre-Upgrade Self-Backup</h2>\n<p>Whenever you trigger an in-panel Nitrobase upgrade under <strong>Settings → Instance</strong>, Nitrobase requires and takes a fresh self-backup to your chosen destination before pulling the new image or running database migrations.</p>\n<div class=\"docCallout docCallout-caution\"><div class=\"docCalloutHeader\"><span class=\"docCalloutBadge\">CAUTION</span><span class=\"docCalloutTitle\">Keep Your ENCRYPTION_KEY Separate</span></div><div class=\"docCalloutContent\">\n<p>The self-backup archive is encrypted with <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>, and the secrets inside the dumped database are also encrypted with <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>. Store your <code>.env</code> (or <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>) in a separate password manager—never in the same bucket as your backups.</p>\n</div></div>"
