    "section": "core-concepts",
    "html": "<p>Nitrobase supports two server connection modes—both execute the exact same Docker, Traefik, backup, and monitoring commands through a unified executor layer.</p>\n<h2>1. Remote Servers (SSH2)</h2>\n<p>Remote Linux servers are managed over <strong>SSH2</strong> (<code>ssh2</code> library):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Authentication:</strong> SSH private key (Ed25519 or RSA, generated inside Nitrobase or imported under <strong>Settings → SSH keys</strong>) or password authentication. All private keys, passphrases, and passwords are encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM (Format v3).</li>\n<li><strong>Host key verification:</strong> Nitrobase verifies the server's SSH host key fingerprint (TOFU—Trust On First Use—with explicit verification on change) to guard against MITM attacks.</li>\n<li><strong>Timeouts &#x26; keepalive:</strong> Configurable via <code>SSH_READY_TIMEOUT_MS</code> (default <code>10s</code>), <code>SSH_KEEPALIVE_MS</code> (<code>10s</code>), <code>COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS</code> (<code>10m</code>), and <code>TERMINAL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS</code> (<code>30m</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>No resident agent:</strong> Nitrobase executes commands, streams logs, collects metrics, and transfers files over SSH/SFTP without installing any background daemon on your VPS.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. Localhost Server (Host Mode)</h2>\n<p>Every fresh Nitrobase installation automatically creates a <strong>Localhost</strong> server entry representing the machine the panel itself runs on.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In <code>docker-compose.prod.yml</code>, <code>nitrobase_app</code> runs with <code>privileged: true</code> and <code>pid: host</code>.</li>\n<li>Controlled by <code>LOCAL_EXEC_MODE</code> (default <code>auto</code>):\n<ul>\n<li><code>auto</code>: Detects whether Nitrobase is running inside a container (<code>/.dockerenv</code>, <code>/run/.containerenv</code>, or cgroup mountinfo) and uses <code>nsenter</code> into PID 1's namespaces to manage the host OS and Docker daemon directly—no SSH loopback required.</li>\n<li><code>container</code>: Always uses <code>nsenter</code>.</li>\n<li><code>host</code>: Executes commands directly on the host (used when running Nitrobase outside Docker, e.g. in development).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"docCallout docCallout-note\"><div class=\"docCalloutHeader\"><span class=\"docCalloutBadge\">NOTE</span><span class=\"docCalloutTitle\">Docker Desktop on macOS / Windows</span></div><div class=\"docCalloutContent\">\n<p>When running Nitrobase on Docker Desktop, the <em>Localhost</em> server refers to Docker's internal Linux VM rather than your macOS or Windows host OS.</p>\n</div></div>"
